### Naming
- Functions are verbs; variables are descriptive nouns. Prefer full words over abbreviations.
- Use meaningful names that remove the need for explanatory comments.

### Types
- `strict` TypeScript; annotate exported/public function signatures. Avoid `any` and unsafe casts.
- Narrow types explicitly; use discriminated unions and enums where appropriate.

### Modules
- ESM only; use `import`/`export`. Prefer named exports. No CommonJS `require`.

### Control Flow & Errors
- Use guard clauses; handle edge cases first; avoid deep nesting.
- Do not catch and ignore errors. Surface actionable messages with provider/context where relevant.

### Async & Streaming
- Plumb `AbortSignal` through handlers/services. Support streaming with backpressure-friendly APIs.

### Comments & Docs
- Use JSDoc for documentation (`/** ... */`); avoid non-standard or noisy comments.
- Document intent (why), not mechanics (how), unless non-obvious.

### Formatting
- Prettier is source of truth. Match existing formatting; wrap long lines; avoid unrelated reformatting.

### Validation & Boundaries
- Validate and sanitize external inputs early (e.g., via `zod`). Convert to internal types in handlers.
- Avoid Node-only APIs on Workers paths; guard conditional imports for cross-runtime code.

### Errors & Utilities
- Prefer centralized error types/utilities in `src/errors/**` and pure helpers in `src/utils/**`.

